($t$Gossypium barbadense$t$, $t$Gossypium barbadense$t$, $t$Malvaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Malvaceae. Portamento: Shrub. Altezza massima indicativa: 3 m. Other known common names are as follows: Extra-long Staple (ELS) cotton, Egyptian cotton, Creole cotton, and pima cotton. Sea island cotton or Gossypium barbadense is a frost-sensitive, tropical, perennial plant with growing as a small and bushy tree of up to 3 m in height. It has yellow flowers and black seeds and it produces cotton with long and silky fibers. These fibers have a wide range of uses including making clothes, rubber-tyre fabrics, stuffing material for pillows and cushions, surgical dressing, twines and ropes, and carpets among others. The seeds are ground into flour and added to bakery products. It yield oil which is used in salads, canned goods, and manufactured into margarine. Root bark infusion is used in the treatment of irregular menstruation. The leaves are used for high blood pressure, abdominal cramps, menstrual problems, etc. The seeds are used for diarrhea and thrush.$t$, $j${"luce": "Pieno sole", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Sea Island Cotton$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Malvaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta":